            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new one: say the Bengali for damp (and dank), then the Bengali for to be covered over."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: কালবৈশাখী",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কালবৈশাখী — kālboishākhī — \"a nor'wester; a spring thunderstorm\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "বিকেলে কালবৈশাখী এসে অনেক গাছ ভেঙে দিল। bikele kālboishākhī ese ônek gāchh bhenge dilô. In the afternoon a nor'wester came and broke many trees."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The sudden violent storms of April and May, in the month of Baishakh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "কালবৈশাখী (kālboishākhī) joins কাল, \"black, deadly\", to বৈশাখী, \"of the month of Baishakh\", from Sanskrit vaiśākha, the spring month (Monier-Williams): the black storm of Baishakh."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for getting around."
            }
          ]
        },
